WEBVTT

00:00:00.344 --> 00:00:01.405
AI just designed

00:00:01.217 --> 00:00:02.478
an entire CPU

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.198
by itself

00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:05.052
Architect Labs calls

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:05.842
it Frostbite

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.611
a general-purpose processor

00:00:07.423 --> 00:00:08.460
with a brand-new

00:00:08.272 --> 00:00:10.159
instruction set discovered

00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:11.621
designed and verified

00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:12.234
end to end

00:00:12.046 --> 00:00:12.835
by their AI

00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:13.425
systems

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:15.882
Across 25 workloads

00:00:15.835 --> 00:00:16.755
15 of them

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:17.627
held back until

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:18.465
the final test

00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:20.505
it delivered 4.59

00:00:20.316 --> 00:00:21.507
times the performance

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:22.038
per watt of

00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:22.616
a modern

00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:24.019
silicon-proven CPU

00:00:23.831 --> 00:00:24.396
core

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.651
A swarm of

00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:27.042
agents tried 58

00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:28.222
design ideas and

00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:29.189
kept 37

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.156
using a chip

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.182
simulator that runs

00:00:30.993 --> 00:00:32.998
660 times faster

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:33.528
than the real

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.283
hardware model

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:35.684
Full story on

00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:36.356
the dashboard
